      ":question/problem": "![](images/5c/5c581f9c0ba307a2d99b5b3c01bfafab1a27f064d6ae6d5e38d64589573e5efc.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $D$ lies on the segment $KM$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OK}=k$ and $\\overrightarrow{OM}=v$. The lengths satisfy $KD:DM=1:2$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OD}$ in terms of $k$ and $v$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OD}=$ {{field-1}} $k+$ {{field-2}} $v$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OK}=k\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OM}=v .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $K$ through $O$ to $M$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{KM}=\\overrightarrow{KO}+\\overrightarrow{OM}=-k+v.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $KD:DM=1:2$ gives $3$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{KD}=\\frac{1}{3}\\overrightarrow{KM}=\\frac{1}{3}(-k+v).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to K\\to D$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OD}&=\\overrightarrow{OK}+\\overrightarrow{KD}\\\\&=k+\\frac{1}{3}(-k+v)\\\\&=\\frac{2}{3}k+\\frac{1}{3}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
